      "content": true,
      "reasons": [
        "narrow: The displayed root-\\(n\\) rate requires every training complement to contain order \\(n\\) observations. Fixed \\(L\\) by itself does not imply this: for example, a two-fold partition may have one training complement of size one. The added fold-balance condition is an estimator-side sampling condition, not a restriction on the observed-law model, and the rest of the claim is unchanged."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "prop:two-period-eif-reduction",
      "change": "changed",
      "fields": [
        "statement"
      ],
      "content": true,
      "reasons": [
        "narrow: The unqualified phrase ``the exhaustive staggered-DDD canonical gradient'' exceeds the proved tangent-exhaustion scope: the frozen canonical-gradient theorem establishes exhaustion only at fixed-finite-support conditional-mean-interior laws and explicitly makes no continuous-covariate canonicality claim. The score identities and the equality \\(\\phi_{\\mathrm{OVS},P}=\\Psi_{k,c,P}\\) are algebraic and remain unrestricted; only their canonical-gradient interpretation is narrowed to the theorem's proved regime."
      ]
    }
